<title>UK: Rolls Royce leads UK engineering shares down.</title>
<headline>Rolls Royce leads UK engineering shares down.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rolls-Royce led shares in UK engineering firms lower on Wednesday as sterling's buoyancy continued to fuel fears that currency strength could hit profits, traders said.</p>
<p>Shares in Rolls-Royce fell 7-1/2p to 225p by 0939 GMT, while Smiths Industries dropped 17p to 745p. Siebe shares traded down 12p to 977-1/2p and TI Group eased three pence at 522p.  </p>
<p>&quot;The engineering sector generally is pretty friendless today,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Sterling was hovering close to 52-month highs against the mark in morning trade after a bigger-than-expected drop in UK January unemployment.</p>
<p>&quot;It's the mark depreciation. You can put most of it down to currency worries,&quot; one analyst said.</p>
<p>-- Simon Gardner, London newsroom + 44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
